  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6d533359-7434-5c2c-8799-66b2761c7620" activityNameId="ddeaf139-1615-533b-b0af-db36cecdbe8c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production ID, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production ID, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 75% of the imported Indonesian natural gas to RoW was imported by pipeline and 25% as LNG. An average distance of 470 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Indonesia, of which are 160 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are  km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=59cde690-0585-37fa-a883-a20670f02c23
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Indonesian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_59cde690-0585-37fa-a883-a20670f02c23.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
